    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as the clear offensive centerpiece, boasting a stellar 82.12 score. His matchup against Feltner is ideal; the combination of a favorable park factor (+14%) and a significant platoon edge (+14%) against a right-hander allows **Pete Crow-Armstrong** to maximize his elite speed potential, a critical metric given our current scarcity strategy for stolen bases. Meanwhile, **Chase Meidroth** (61.90) secures his spot as a strong play at the top of the lineup; hitting leadoff against P\u00e9rez, M provides the necessary volume of plate appearances to offset his more modest base projection, while his 10% bonus for occupying the #1 spot makes him a high-floor asset in this rotation.\n\nConversely, the lineup construction faced a squeeze at the UTIL position, where **Carson Benge** (53.20) edged out our depth options to make the final start. While **Colt Keith** (58.22) also presents a strong play due to his platoon advantage against Matthews, the most notable decision remains the preservation of game caps amidst a sparse schedule. We are currently navigating a day where impact bats like **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, **Trea Turner**, and **Kyle Schwarber** are all sidelined by off-days, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining active roster. Caution is advised with **Luke Raley** (54.19), whose respectable score is currently dampened by a 42% rain risk that threatens his ability to complete a full game; should he be scratched, we have **Christian Yelich** and **Caleb Durbin** on standby to mitigate the risk. We are also monitoring **Dillon Dingler** (44.03), who faces a tough assignment against Matthews, though his presence in the heart of the order and the potential for a slow delivery from the opposing pitcher keep him just above our benching threshold.",
